<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.12.7: Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01957</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.12.7: Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c7ab0c14-9e97-4e08-9ba8-f3b181af69ac</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Explain how the \(a\) and \(c\) in \(ax^2+bx+c\) affect the graph of the equation. </item>
  <item> Explain how graphs, tables, and equations that represent the same quadratic function are related. </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 7.12.1: Using Coefficients and Constant Terms to Identify Graphs of Linear Equations </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you matched three linear equations with their graphs by comparing slopes and \(y\)-intercepts. </item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.12.2: Transformations with Quadratic Functions </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you explored how transformations affect the graphs of quadratic functions. </item>
    <item> 7.12.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 7.12.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.12.3: Understanding the Behaviors of a Graph in Relation to Its Quadratic Expression </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you examined the values in tables and how the values from a quadratic expression affect its graph. </item>
    <item> 7.12.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 7.12.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.12.4: Representations of Quadratic Functions </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you used the standard form and factored form of quadratic functions as well as their graphs to identify intercepts to match the equivalent forms and their graphs. </item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.12.4: Self Check </item>
  <list>
    <item> 7.12.4: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.12.5: Identifying Graphs of Quadratic Equations </item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you matched the graphs of quadratic functions with their equations. </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para>After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list>
  <item> 7.12.6: Practice </item>
</list>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Checking In</title><exercise data-content-id="e6226166-f14b-4a92-83ca-75f5f8b4bed8"><problem><para>
      <para>On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson? </para>
    </para></problem><solution><newline/><para>
      <para>Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
